course: dictionary
lesson: 13783
title: Medical words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word intravenously is built from two parts. Intra means inside, and venous means to do with a vein. Veins are the tubes that carry blood around your body. So intravenously means into a vein.
explain: Look at the clues in «The nurse gave the fluid intravenously, through a tiny tube in her arm.» The words through a tiny tube in her arm show that the fluid goes into the body, not into the mouth. Swap in your meaning: "The nurse gave the fluid by putting it straight into a vein." It still makes sense, so you have understood it.
explain: Intravenously is an adverb, because it tells you how something is done. «Fed intravenously» tells you the food was not eaten or drunk. It went in through a vein.
fact: Intravenously is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens.
fact: Intravenously means by putting something straight into a vein, usually with a needle or drip.
fact: «Fed intravenously» means food or fluid goes straight into the blood through a vein.
fact: Doctors use this way when medicine needs to reach the blood fast.
fact: Intravenous is the adjective form, as in «an intravenous drip».
exercise: «The nurse gave the medicine intravenously, through a drip.» How was the medicine given? | By mouth, with a spoon | Wrapped in a bandage | *Straight into a vein | Rubbed onto the skin
exercise: «The patient was fed intravenously because she could not eat.» What does intravenously mean here? | *By putting food straight into a vein | Very quickly, like a race | Sitting up in bed | Through the nose
exercise: «The doctor gave the injection intravenously.» Find and copy the word that tells how the injection was given. | gave | injection | doctor | *intravenously
test: Intravenously is which part of speech? | Adjective | Noun | *Adverb | Verb
test: Ben says intravenously means very slowly. What is the right meaning? | *Straight into a vein, usually with a needle or drip | Through the skin | Inside a box | Very slowly
exam: «The drip carried fluid intravenously into Maya's arm.» Which words show where the fluid went? | Carried fluid | *Into Maya's arm, through the drip | Maya's name | The fluid was sad
